A||||6||Fformula88||Dunlop SP Sport A2's... anybody got 'em?||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||09-07-2001||11:19 PM||||I've had a pair on the rear of my Fiero for about a month now.  They are supposedly the replacement to the D60 A2's (I loved those tires, great grip!).  These new ones seem even better to me!  I still have a good pair of D60A2's on the front, and yet they seem to start slipping long before the SP Sport A2's start to loose their grip.<P>Anybody else have them?  What do you think abou them.  I'd imagine having them on all 4 corners would induce a lot of grins!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000001||Brian87egotrip||09-07-2001||11:21 PM||||i have the sp5000  oohhh i love them. Great traction<P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||09-08-2001||01:30 AM||||I have 215/45/17 SP Sport W10s, like 'em rightly enough, but I will be switching to PZero Pirellis once they wear down (and once the bank account recovers from what I'm doing to the silver car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The Dunlops are nice though, very liniar breakage, you can slide the car around nicely (for a tiny little while, with a clutch dump, then they just GRIP  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||09-08-2001||07:40 AM||||I had Dunlops on my Mercedes SL and was very satisfied. They were OEM tires, most people think Mercedes only uses Michelin.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||09-08-2001||12:53 PM||||The Perelli's will be nice!  I have a set of P4000's on my 97 Probe and they are a great all around tire.  A lot more grip than I would have expected (they are Super-Touring tires, not outright performance).  Plus they are good in the wet and absolutely awesome in snow! <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">   <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||09-08-2001||01:03 PM||||I just got a pair of Yokohoma Avid H4's put on the front of the quad.  Haven't had a chance to really put them through their paces yet, but so far I'm really impressed with the traction and ride comfort.  Took some harshness out of the front end and reduced the steering effort, too.  Very nice tires, and at 54 bucks for 205/60 15 a pretty good deal, too.  and they're directional  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroKyle||09-08-2001||01:18 PM||||I love my Goodyear Eagle GT 2 tires. They are 215/60/14 all around. They stick anything that has asphalt. Plue with the white lettering they look good too. Before them, it had Kelly Chargers on and they sucked ass. I had one tire that tore completely apart. The Chargers is what I bought the car with. See Sig.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign_1.jpg">  <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>AOL Name: Yakty Yak<BR>E-Mail: YaktyYak@aol.com<P>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
